-- title:
--   Functoriality of the crossing model in the coefficient ring
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ and $W'$ be commutative rings (in the base universe), let $\rho : W \simeq W'$ be a ring isomorphism, and let $\pi \in W$. Write $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,\pi$ for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, W)$ by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - C(\pi)$, i.e. $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi)$; here $U\,\pi$ and $V\,\pi$ denote the classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$, and $\mathrm{const}\,\pi\,w$ denotes the class of the constant series $C(w)$ for $w \in W$. The assertion is that there exists a ring isomorphism $$\theta : W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi) \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; W'[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\rho(\pi))$$ such that $\theta(U\,\pi) = U\,(\rho\pi)$, $\theta(V\,\pi) = V\,(\rho\pi)$, and $\theta(\mathrm{const}\,\pi\,w) = \mathrm{const}\,(\rho\pi)\,(\rho w)$ for every $w \in W$; that is, $\theta$ carries each coordinate to the coordinate of the same index and acts on constants through $\rho$. Only existence of such a $\theta$ is asserted, with no uniqueness or continuity claim.
--
--   This records that the formal model of an ordinary double point, $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi)$, depends on the coefficient ring only up to isomorphism, in a way compatible with the two coordinates and with constants. It is used in the construction of crossing-model presentations of completed local rings on modular curves, where the coefficient ring is first identified with a completion and the presentation is then transported along that identification.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_ringEquiv_apply_U_apply_V_apply_const_of_ringEquiv.lean

